course: dictionary
lesson: 12719
title: The downside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A downside is the bad part of something that is mostly good. It is the catch. «The new bike is fast, but the downside is that it is very heavy to carry up the stairs.» The bike is fast, which is good. The heavy part is the downside.
explain: The opposite is the upside, the good part of something. When people make a decision, they often list the upsides and downsides first. This is called weighing up the pros and cons.
explain: Look for the phrases «the downside is» and «on the downside». They warn you that a bad point is coming, even when the rest of the sentence sounds great. «On the downside, the park closes at six.»
fact: A downside is the bad part or disadvantage of something that is mostly good.
fact: The downside of a plan is what could go wrong or what it costs you.
fact: «The downside is» tells the reader that a catch is coming.
fact: Upside and downside are opposites: the upside is the good part, the downside is the bad part.
fact: Debates and persuasive writing often list upsides and downsides before a decision is made.
exercise: «The new game is fun, but the downside is that it uses up a lot of battery.» What is the downside here? | The game is fun | The game was free | *The game uses up a lot of battery | The game has bright colours
exercise: What is the downside of a plan? | The colour it is written in | The people who made it | The best part of it | *What could go wrong or what it costs you
exercise: «On the downside, the trip to the beach means an early start.» What does the phrase «on the downside» tell you? | The beach is closed | A good point is coming | *A bad point is coming | The trip is cancelled
test: Which word is the opposite of downside? | Drawback | Disadvantage | *Upside | Catch
test: «The school trip is great, but the downside is the long bus ride.» What is the downside? | The great fun | The school trip | Being at school | *The long bus ride
exam: Ben lists the upsides and downsides of getting a pet. Which one is a downside? | *It needs daily walks and costs money | It is always happy to see you | It is fun to play with | It is soft and warm
